"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 5.8 and positive surgical margins. The pathological findings show an ISUP grade group 2 (Gleason 3+4) with pT2 disease, but the presence of lymph node metastasis is concerning. Seminal vesicle invasion was absent, which is favorable. A key countervailing finding is that there was no extraprostatic extension and no documented seminal vesicle invasion. The biopsy-to-prostatectomy comparison is limited as the Gleason pattern and ISUP report from the initial biopsy are missing. Missing information regarding postoperative PSA trajectory would significantly revise this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 62.79 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 50.23–75.35 months; its coverage has not been validated."
